WEBVTT

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.520
Spider-Man!

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.000
The new adventures of Spider-Man.

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:08.900
Today we present the sinister plan of the Dr. Octopus

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:21.390
This is life, without traffic lights, without congestion, without problems

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.080
Go, go, talking about problems

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.200
New York Cultural Museum

00:01:27.620 --> 00:01:30.000
That sounded like someone getting into the museum

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:33.010
And if I'm not mistaken, that's illegal.

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:39.640
Let's take some pictures for the clarinet while the spider does its thing.

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:15.430
I did it! Only the mechanical arms of Doctor Octopus could steal this ruby of a million dollars.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:21.510
And only the flexible spider web of Spider-Man will make you wish you had never tried it.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:22.640
You!

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:28.580
Wow! What a rude way to greet!

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.400
Stop worrying, villain.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.850
The spider is here!

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:45.800
What do I have to do to get rid of you?

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:53.140
Why don't you try eating some onions?

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:57.340
That's the only reason I'll quit your club of admirers.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:00.000
Now that the insect doesn't bother me anymore,

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:04.740
Continue with my master plan to steal me from the world!

00:03:04.740 --> 00:03:10.740
How I miss the Inocites!

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:19.240
I don't understand, why Doctor Octopus stole that ruby but left all the other jewels?

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:38.080
Oh no, I forgot my homework. The professor will punish me for this.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:46.880
I can barely keep my eyes open...

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:57.590
Poor Peter, I hope he hasn't spent the night doing his homework again.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:02.000
It's time to get up.

00:04:03.410 --> 00:04:04.430
Oh no...

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:08.860
If Aunt May sees me with the Spider-Man suit, she'll make me puke.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:19.210
Aunt May, I think... I fell asleep.

00:04:19.210 --> 00:04:21.930
Don't be late for school.

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:24.940
God helps those who wake up early.

00:04:24.940 --> 00:04:28.840
Uh, speaking of other things, is there something on the radio about Doctor Octopus?

00:04:28.840 --> 00:04:30.000
Who, darling?

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:35.240
Look at that! Those red socks you're wearing are adorable!

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:39.040
Uh, yeah, I think I was in the mood for something more colorful.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:42.640
Good. You wash your teeth and behind your ears well.

00:04:42.640 --> 00:04:45.240
Yeah, of course. Thanks for reminding me.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:50.760
Oh, Aunt May, never scare me like that again.

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:55.910
I have to finish my homework about historical places in New York or they're going to reprimand me.

00:04:56.250 --> 00:05:00.000
And the only way Peter Parker gets here

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:07.160
The library is like the friendly spider man of the neighborhood.

00:05:07.160 --> 00:05:11.850
University Empire State.

00:05:11.850 --> 00:05:16.740
Now I will steal the second object I need for my master plan.

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:38.400
It's even weirder that I'm in a hurry. I only have two hours to finish my task.

00:05:39.150 --> 00:05:42.430
Uh-oh, my arachnid sense is activating.

00:05:42.970 --> 00:05:44.550
Well, goodbye task.

00:05:48.910 --> 00:06:00.000
I'm going to do something, I'm going to call security.

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:03.600
Don't worry, this looks like a job for a blacksmith.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:08.300
Spider-Man, you have to help us! Try to steal our valuable lunar rock!

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:12.760
Yes, of course. Now that you need me, I'm the wonderful man, right?

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:15.910
Done! Maybe that'll stop him.

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:22.630
Hey! Don't do that! Let go of me! Let go of me!

00:06:22.630 --> 00:06:28.160
Damn, I have to be more careful with what I say.

00:06:28.160 --> 00:06:30.000
Agreed, Doc.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:32.300
If that's how you want us to do it...

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:41.100
Now I've got my foot in it.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:42.900
Doc Ock was smarter than I was.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.600
He used his metal arms for remote control.

00:06:46.010 --> 00:06:48.270
I think he managed to escape, Spider-Man.

00:06:48.460 --> 00:06:53.260
Fortunately, he left the invaluable lunar rock and took a piece of worthless quartz by accident.

00:06:53.260 --> 00:06:54.570
Don't believe it, miss.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:56.570
Dr. Octopus doesn't make mistakes.

00:06:56.870 --> 00:07:00.000
That fragment of quartz interested him more than the lunar rock.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:02.980
...and it depends on me to find out why.

00:07:02.980 --> 00:07:07.650
Let's see, um...

00:07:07.650 --> 00:07:11.110
Historic places of New York, huh? Here they are.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:16.260
Hello?

00:07:16.260 --> 00:07:18.620
Oh, how are you, Mr. Jameson?

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.120
Oh, I'm very well, as never. I want to talk to Peter.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:24.630
I'm sorry, Mr. Jameson. He's studying. Can I...

00:07:24.630 --> 00:07:26.130
Studying? What do you mean studying?

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:29.130
They just stole a diamond! I want a report!

00:07:29.130 --> 00:07:30.000
I think you have...

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.500
You'll have to ask someone else, Mr. Jameson. Peter must finish his task. Thank you for calling.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:41.560
It was nothing.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:42.560
What was that, Aunt Mel?

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:47.560
Oh, nothing, Peter. Just Mr. Jameson and something about a robbery in the diamond store.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:54.130
It must be something big if the man decided to call in person.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:57.130
If the doc is behind the robbery, only the spider will stop him.

00:08:14.430 --> 00:08:21.380
Suddenly, a strange and powerful tentacle took the diamond and disappeared through the duct of the air.

00:08:22.430 --> 00:08:25.150
It's definitely Doc Ock, but I don't understand it.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:28.000
Stealing small jewelry fragments is not his style.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.000
I have to find out what he's really looking for.

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:52.160
Ready. My tentacles are now ten times more powerful than they were before.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:56.840
I'm finally ready to put my most daring plan into action!

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:00.000
There's no trace of Dohko.

00:09:03.680 --> 00:09:05.080
You're the Spider-Man!

00:09:05.080 --> 00:09:06.080
What's going on?

00:09:06.080 --> 00:09:07.080
He's going down the sewer!

00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:08.080
Hey, Spider-Man!

00:09:08.080 --> 00:09:15.770
I'm sorry, friends. There's no time for autographs, but you can applaud if you want.

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:19.010
No wonder no one found his hideout.

00:09:19.010 --> 00:09:22.080
I hope he stays.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.230
My arachnid sense sounds like an alarm.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:27.470
This is where I'll leave my camera.

00:09:31.790 --> 00:09:37.150
How strange, there is no one here, but my arachnid sense has never been wrong before.

00:09:37.150 --> 00:09:40.700
And he is not wrong now Spider-Man.

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:44.500
Thank you, you give me the welcome with open arms, Doc.

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:48.260
It will be the last welcome you will have, Wall Climber.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:50.590
Do you have your last words?

00:09:50.590 --> 00:09:54.790
Ugh, if it's not much trouble, I'll start by saying:

00:09:54.790 --> 00:09:56.570
Help!

00:09:56.570 --> 00:09:59.860
I'm tired of your jokes, Spider-Man.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:03.250
Are you sure? I already told you that joke about...

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:07.630
Hey! I cut you off, I was telling you a joke.

00:10:07.630 --> 00:10:12.200
Well, a little spider web will stop you.

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:15.110
How bad, it was filled with water.

00:10:15.110 --> 00:10:20.870
What a pity Spider-Man, but my deadly tentacles are a test of water.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:26.110
And this quartz sonic vibrator will paralyze you.

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:30.000
Ah! I can almost...

00:10:30.030 --> 00:10:39.550
You are very lucky, you will be the first to see my new tentacles in action, like this diamond saw.

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:46.730
Thank you for the show, I missed the ads.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:52.730
I'm sorry, Trepamuros, the show is over for you, forever!

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:03.880
I'm already bathed, Doc. Besides, I don't bathe without my ule duck.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:12.620
If I don't break these bars, it'll be the end of Spider-Man.

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:15.240
I can't even move them.

00:11:15.630 --> 00:11:21.250
If I don't free myself, it'll be the end of Spider-Man.

00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:24.100
And even worse, I won't finish my task.

00:11:41.520 --> 00:11:57.680
Now I will raise the periscope and look for my first defenseless white, there it is, a cargo ship, full of millions of barrels of oil, now it leads to the final base of my master plan, first my laser tentacle will stop the ship

00:12:02.880 --> 00:12:05.220
We give you power!

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:09.050
Excellent. Now I will immobilize the crew.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:16.280
It's useless. We have to call the Coast Guard.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:23.810
My diamond drill will cut this cargo as if it were butter.

00:12:23.810 --> 00:12:30.000
Now I just have to pump the oil to my secret tanks. Soon.

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:35.090
But I will control all the oil in the world, and with it, I will control the world.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:39.690
I never thought I would envy a golden fish.

00:12:39.690 --> 00:12:43.740
That's just what I was looking for: a bottle of acid.

00:12:43.740 --> 00:12:46.170
But how will I reach it?

00:12:46.170 --> 00:12:50.510
A spider web is my only opportunity.

00:12:50.510 --> 00:12:52.510
Do not fail now, spider web.

00:12:52.510 --> 00:12:59.650
I have it! It has to work. There is no time for a second attempt.

00:13:07.200 --> 00:13:09.330
I'll never shower again!

00:13:09.330 --> 00:13:10.160
Uh-oh!

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.360
I hope the water doesn't damage the film.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:14.560
Well, I can't worry about that.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:16.560
Not with that six-armed madman.

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:23.260
This is useless, De Parker, when I need all the available photographers!

00:13:23.260 --> 00:13:27.270
All the oil in New York is disappearing under our noses

00:13:27.270 --> 00:13:28.970
and he has to do his job.

00:13:28.970 --> 00:13:30.000
But Uncle Jonah...

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:34.420
Who needs Parker's alcornoque? I'll get you the photos you need!

00:13:34.420 --> 00:13:39.420
Oh, hehe, good idea Mortimer, take the helicopter of the clarin!

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:40.310
I'll do it!

00:13:40.310 --> 00:13:48.330
Miss Brandt, call Parker again, and if you answer your aunt, tell her it was the wrong number.

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:52.190
There is no sign of Doctor Octopus anywhere.

00:13:52.190 --> 00:13:56.880
Extra! About the mysterious disappearance of the oil!

00:13:56.880 --> 00:14:00.000
Did my delicate ears hear that?

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:02.980
Buy your diary here, the clarin!

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:11.560
The diary! The diary!

00:14:11.560 --> 00:14:17.260
According to a report from the Coast Guard, the freighters are mysteriously stripped of their oil?

00:14:17.260 --> 00:14:20.640
I saw you suppose it, that's what Octopus is up to.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:24.500
Uh-oh, my locator, it must be Aunt May.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:27.650
What's going on, Aunt May?

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:30.000
Ender, where did you go all of a sudden?

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:32.380
I had more things to investigate.

00:14:32.380 --> 00:14:36.380
I hope you don't study too much, I don't want you to get tired.

00:14:36.380 --> 00:14:39.380
Eh, no, I'm taking it easy, Aunt May.

00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:44.380
But not too much calm, I want you to get a 10 in your homework.

00:14:44.380 --> 00:14:50.320
Oh no, but what a big mess, my Doc Ock track and at this point I'm not going to finish my homework either.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:52.530
How do I tell Aunt May?

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:56.550
Hey, wait a minute, why didn't it happen to me before?

00:14:56.550 --> 00:15:00.000
If I can synchronize my radio with the frequency of the oscillator,

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:04.000
Dr. Octopus' ultrasonic beam, maybe I can locate him.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:09.200
It works!

00:15:09.200 --> 00:15:11.400
Very good, Doc!

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:15.150
Ready or not, here I come!

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:17.090
There are no disturbances anywhere!

00:15:17.090 --> 00:15:20.140
I have to take those pictures to beat Peter Parker!

00:15:20.140 --> 00:15:21.970
Hey, what's that?

00:15:21.970 --> 00:15:22.970
It's Spider-Man!

00:15:22.970 --> 00:15:25.760
Quick, follow Trepamuro, he's good for nothing!

00:15:31.150 --> 00:15:35.390
These ships have no defenses against my super powerful tentacles.

00:15:35.390 --> 00:15:38.230
Hmm, everything looks normal from here.

00:15:38.230 --> 00:15:41.680
I'll put my camera down and go down to investigate.

00:15:41.680 --> 00:15:46.040
Wow, this octopus has more tricks under the tentacles than a magician.

00:15:46.040 --> 00:15:49.560
But the Spider-Man also knows some tricks.

00:15:49.560 --> 00:15:54.800
The oil flow stopped. Something got stuck.

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:56.530
I'll check the surface.

00:16:01.080 --> 00:16:02.020
Spider-Man!

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:06.700
I will get rid of that intruded insect once and for all!

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:11.630
Good morning, neighbor. I am the welcome committee.

00:16:12.090 --> 00:16:16.190
Forget the useless. Nothing can penetrate the atomic glass that I invented.

00:16:19.170 --> 00:16:22.250
Why do I face the most dangerous criminal of all again?

00:16:22.610 --> 00:16:24.610
Idea that examines my head.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:27.400
Hey, look! It's Doctor Octopus!

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.000
He's giving a beating to Spider-Man!

00:16:31.560 --> 00:16:35.780
Hey Doc! If you keep going like this, it will be the end of our beautiful friendship!

00:16:40.260 --> 00:16:45.620
Oh! A little further down and I didn't count it...

00:16:45.620 --> 00:16:54.420
Now you went too far!

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:07.400
Spider-Man was defeated and for the first time I arrived before Peter Parker.

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:10.980
My uncle Jonas will be very happy when he sees all the photos I took.

00:17:10.980 --> 00:17:13.760
Someone is spying on me from the helicopter.

00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:15.950
This will stop him.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:22.440
Doctor Octopus! He discovered us! Let's get out of here!

00:17:22.440 --> 00:17:27.810
Oh no! He caught us!

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:43.290
I'll be full of sharks!

00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:52.410
If you don't stop fighting, I'll put you in a fish tank!

00:17:52.410 --> 00:17:56.550
Oh no!

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:59.600
Topus caught Mortimer in the helicopter of the clarin!

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.200
It's not worth separating them, those two are just like that.

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:26.090
I'll teach those intruders not to spy on Dr. Octopus, huh?

00:18:26.090 --> 00:18:29.440
Let's get out of here!

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:34.450
I have to go back to the clearing!

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:36.110
Damn!

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:37.760
That's just what I was waiting for.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:41.240
Now I just have to fool Octopus so he can go there?

00:18:41.240 --> 00:18:44.680
Yes, I'll do that.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:49.970
That scurvy spider won't be believing that he can get away from me so easily.

00:19:03.610 --> 00:19:07.590
You don't have any more tricks, Trepamuros! It's over here!

00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:10.170
You're right about that, Doc!

00:19:10.170 --> 00:19:22.310
What's going on, octopus? Did the mouse eat your tongue?

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:28.230
Captain Gerard of the United States Navy. We're in charge of this, Spider-Man.

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.060
Uncle Jonah! Hey, Uncle Jonah!

00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:42.920
What do you want? Don't you see that I'm...

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:44.920
Oh, Mortimer, it's you!

00:19:44.920 --> 00:19:46.920
I bring good news!

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:48.920
I took several photos of Doctor Octopus

00:19:48.920 --> 00:19:50.920
making pieces of Spider-Man!

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:52.920
Spider-Man in pieces? Don't stay there!

00:19:52.920 --> 00:19:54.920
Show them to me!

00:19:54.920 --> 00:19:56.920
I haven't even seen them, Uncle Jonah! I brought them from the lab!

00:20:00.640 --> 00:20:02.640
What? These photos are in white!

00:20:02.640 --> 00:20:05.640
Is it a Mortimer joke?

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.640
Oh no! The laser shot must have ruined them!

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:10.640
I swear they were incredible, Uncle Jonah!

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.640
Doctor Octopus sunk Spider-Man in the bottom of the sea!

00:20:13.640 --> 00:20:18.110
How curious, that's not what I saw.

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:21.110
It was Spider-Man who sunk the poor octopus.

00:20:21.110 --> 00:20:23.480
Let's see, yes...

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:26.880
These photos are very good, Parker.

00:20:26.880 --> 00:20:30.000
If you hadn't wasted your time with your task, maybe it would be...

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:35.250
Caracoles, I forgot my homework. I'll submit it in 10 minutes. I think I'll fail the class.

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:40.050
Well, you don't always win, kid. The important thing is that we have these pictures of the Spider-Man

00:20:40.050 --> 00:20:42.250
climbing all over New York.

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:47.330
All over New York. That's it. See you later, JJ.

00:20:47.330 --> 00:20:52.160
But what? Where are you going with my pictures, Parker?

00:20:52.160 --> 00:20:57.180
Peter, you got a 10 in your history class. I'm sure you did an excellent report.

00:20:57.180 --> 00:21:00.000
Well, actually, I didn't write it.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:03.780
a report aunt May. I used the photos that I took for the clarinet and I did a

00:21:03.780 --> 00:21:07.980
graphic essay of the historical points of the city. The teacher loved it.

00:21:07.980 --> 00:21:13.380
They are adorable Peter, but they would have been perfect if that horrible spider man

00:21:13.380 --> 00:21:17.090
would not have appeared in every and every one.
